# SE2CAD core

The repository is durable engineering truth. Conversation history is not. A fresh session must read repository state, not rely on prior chat.

## Authority

The human architect exclusively owns architecture changes, project scope, technology-selection changes, plan unit sequencing or creation/removal, significant tradeoffs, licensing, third-party publishing, and all git commit, tag, push, release, and deployment actions.

Within one explicitly authorized bounded unit, an agent may inspect the repo, change files the unit requires, add tests, verify, assess, remediate verified defects, and update durable state.

## Stop conditions

Stop and report to the human architect if correct work needs an architectural decision, meaningful scope expansion, a new plan unit, or a licensing/provenance judgment.

Also stop and report if:

- repository documentation and implementation conflict in a way that changes the design;
- two materially different implementations are both defensible and choosing between them requires a significant architectural or technology tradeoff;
- a quality/security finding requires a design change rather than a local fix.

Do not silently change architecture. Do not expand scope because adjacent work looks useful. Do not invent roadmap units while executing a unit.

## Publication

Do not commit, tag, push, publish, or release unless the human architect explicitly asks in that session.

